   00059| # Issue #1072: every node used to extract a full `git archive` (966 MB, most of
   00060| # it `dev/` and `docs/` evidence) into a fresh temporary directory, `git init`
   00061| # it, and commit it -- then compile there. Measured on run 34326451343: 110
   00062| # minutes for 32 leaves, 25 of them Agent CLI work. Two costs made up the rest:
   00063| # copying and re-hashing a gigabyte per node, and a workspace path cargo had
   00064| # never seen, so every leaf recompiled the crate from scratch, shared target
   00065| # directory or not. The fresh `git init` also minted a new root commit per
   00066| # node, which is the project identity `@link-assistant/agent` keys its
   00067| # snapshot store on: 115 stores, 31 GB, in six hours.
   00068| #
   00069| # One worktree, created once at one path, sparse so the evidence trees are
   00070| # never checked out, and reset between nodes. Same path, so the second leaf's
   00071| # `cargo check` is incremental; same root commit, so one snapshot store.
   00072| BASE_SHA=$(git -C "$ROOT" rev-parse HEAD)
   00073| git -C "$ROOT" worktree add --detach --no-checkout "$WORK" "$BASE_SHA" >/dev/null
   00074| git -C "$WORK" sparse-checkout init --no-cone >/dev/null
   00075| # `dev/` is 693 MB of captured logs and nothing compiles from it. `docs/` has
   00076| # to stay: 31 `include_str!` call sites in the test suite read
   00077| # `docs/case-studies/`, one of them from a `raw-data/` log, so excluding it
   00078| # made `cargo test` fail to compile inside the node -- which the harness
   00079| # scored as the leaf's own `failing_leaf_tests` rather than as its own
   00080| # breakage. `docs/assets/` holds only images no source reads.
   00081| # `dev/` is 693 MB of captured logs, but the test suite compiles exactly one
   00082| # file out of it (`issue_991_incremental_decomposition.rs` reads a learning
   00083| # report through `include_str!`), so that one path is added back. `docs/` has
   00084| # to stay whole: 31 `include_str!` sites read `docs/case-studies/`, one of them
   00085| # a `raw-data/` log. Excluding either made `cargo test` fail to compile inside
   00086| # the node, which the harness scored as the leaf's own `failing_leaf_tests`
   00087| # rather than as the harness's breakage -- a false verdict about Formal AI.
   00088| # `docs/assets/` holds only images no source reads.
   00089| sparse_paths=('/*' '!/dev/' '/dev/log/issues/702/pulls/818/agent-cli/' '!/docs/assets/')
   00090| if [[ "$AUTHORED_RULES" == disabled ]]; then
   00091|   # These 32 documents and leaves.tsv contain exact leaf-to-edit mappings. The
   00092|   # harness reads its oracle from ROOT before invoking the agent, while the
   00093|   # repository worktree presented to the agent omits both forms of the answer.
   00094|   # Sparse exclusion keeps the worktree clean, unlike deleting tracked files
   00095|   # after checkout, so the unchanged diff judge remains identical in both
   00096|   # modes.
   00097|   sparse_paths+=(
   00098|     '!/experiments/issue_1028_agent_cli_ladder/rules/'
   00099|     '!/experiments/issue_1028_agent_cli_ladder/leaves.tsv'
   00100|   )
   00101| fi
   00102| git -C "$WORK" sparse-checkout set --no-cone "${sparse_paths[@]}" >/dev/null
   00103| git -C "$WORK" checkout -q --detach "$BASE_SHA"
   00104| git -C "$WORK" config user.email agent-ladder@example.invalid
   00105| git -C "$WORK" config user.name agent-ladder
